,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":10.883454148,"data":"[eda] 4,407 training studies, 24,371 training series, 15 test series\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":10.884366425,"data":"[eda] 58 studies carry all twelve labels; the rest are supervised only by what a text model read out of the report\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538512352,"data":"Coverage of the six slots the models expect, over training studies:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538536034,"data":"               slot  studies with it  share\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538539404,"data":"   Sagittal fat-sat             4150  0.942\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.53854244,"data":"Sagittal no fat-sat             4266  0.968\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538559699,"data":"    Coronal fat-sat             4248  0.964\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538563569,"data":" Coronal no fat-sat             3406  0.773\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538567574,"data":"      Axial fat-sat             4407  1.000\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538571357,"data":"   Axial no fat-sat              857  0.194\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538575567,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":11.538580418,"data":"A slot no study fills is a column of zeros fed to the encoder; a study that fills none of them can only be given a constant, and under ROC-AUC a block of identical constants earns half credit against everything it ties with. That is the cheapest score leak in this whole pipeline.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.00342202,"data":"Most correlated pairs:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.003465473,"data":"  Medial OA          + Baker's            +0.48\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.003471578,"data":"  Medial Meniscus    + Medial OA          +0.42\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.003475789,"data":"  Lateral Meniscus   + Lateral OA         +0.42\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.003480041,"data":"  Lateral Meniscus   + Medial OA          +0.41\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.003485004,"data":"  Lateral OA         + Baker's            +0.40\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.003489139,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12.003493753,"data":"The three osteoarthritis compartments move together, which is why the calibrator downstream groups them. Findings that co-occur are also findings an ensemble tends to get right or wrong together — worth remembering before reading any per-finding weight as skill.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":13.01878938,"data":"0 studies have no report at all (0.0%) — those can only be supervised by the images.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":13.01882488,"data":"The counts overlap because clinical vocabulary is shared across languages; they are a rough shape, not a classifier. The point is that a monolingual extractor silently drops whole slices of the training set, and a dropped study is not a wrong label — it is no label.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":14.426328851,"data":"A 140 mm crop spans 398 to 896 pixels across these series — a 2.3x range. Cropping a fixed number of pixels instead would hand the model a different anatomical field of view per scanner, which is the kind of artefact a model will happily learn to read as signal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":21.670198363,"data":"Field strengths present: 1.5T x144, 3.0T x90, 1.2T x2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":21.670259921,"data":"The single most common scanner model covers 23% of the sample.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":21.670267646,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":21.670273721,"data":"The training path in this notebook groups folds by md5(report text), which deduplicates identical reports but does nothing about the scanner. Manufacturer + model + matrix size + pixel spacing is a serviceable site key and costs nothing to compute from headers you are already reading. Grouping on it is what makes an offline number mean something.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":22.023409892,"data":"Median series length 30 slices; 0.0% are shorter than twelve.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":22.023449865,"data":"Where a series is shorter than its slot, the sampler repeats slices, so several of the 62 windows are duplicates and the attention pooling sees the same evidence more than once. Where a series is much longer, the sampler is skipping anatomy — and a meniscus tear visible on two slices can fall between samples entirely. That is the mechanism behind the max and top-2 window pooling used for the focal findings upstream.\n"}
